Vita: choose at start-up between Inline FIFO processing (the default, as patch 0001 set it) and
upstream's Thread mode, where a worker processes the FIFO, and so runs every backend draw, while the
game thread goes on encoding commands.

drain() (GXDrawDone, aurora_end_frame) still waits for the worker, so the GX state, the game's
memory the commands point at and the frame's order are the same in both modes; only J3D's command
encoding overlaps the processing. std::thread gets VitaSDK's 32 KiB default stack, too small for the
backend's draw path, so the Vita worker is a pthread with a 512 KiB stack; the backend's
twv_gx_worker_started hook gives it its core. The 0001 lock elisions now test the mode at run time.

